# Incidence geometry of the canonical radial target cells

The cells indexed by consecutive binary addresses form a genuine cyclic
closed cover of a standard polygonal shell.  This file establishes the
boundary avoidance and pairwise interior-disjointness needed before their
marked disk homeomorphisms can be glued.
